# Local OpenTofu state + provider plugins for the operator-owned k8s-IT stages
# (cluster/, infra/, shared-scenario/) — never commit.
#
# `make destroy` tears infra + the cluster down; `make clean` wipes the local files
# entirely. Both are operator-initiated: the ITs never call them.
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
terraform.tfstate
terraform.tfstate.backup
*.tfvars.local
crash.log
crash.*.log

# kind-written kubeconfig (cluster/sutra-fednow-it-config) — contains the cluster CA
# + client cert/key. The tehcyx/kind provider writes it as <cluster_name>-config in
# cluster/. Never commit credentials. (The bare name is kept alongside the glob: it is
# the harness's hardcoded default path.)
*-config
sutra-fednow-it-config

# Observability access dump written by the infra stage's null_resource — contains the
# live LB IPs AND the elastic superuser password. Never commit credentials.
observability-access.txt
